Security integration contract
-----------------------------
Run node patches/dsh/patch-host.mjs RUNTIME_DIRECTORY exactly once after
installation, before starting DSH. Unknown versions, altered inputs and
already-patched files are rejected. All discovered pnpm package copies are
validated before writes. Preserve patched packages on the immutable rootfs.
The patched WebServer always requires an access gate from first accept.
registerRequiredAccessGate({http,upgrade}) is synchronous and exclusive;
requiredAccessGateVersion is required-access-gate-v1. Missing gate: HTTP 503.
Gate exceptions clear registration and close accepted sockets; disposal clears
registration and closes HTTP streams, keepalive and upgraded sockets. No
private server listener takeover, relay, custom parser, or unguarded fallback.

Activate the bundle @soulwhisper/dsh-sso in every served profile; the patch
inserts required Host-only distribution-sso with webServer+connection injection.
The app-boot exact patch adds distribution-sso to requiredStartupEntryIds,
the native required-entry policy (Loader has no required:true row property).
DSH_SSO_ALLOWED_UIDS is a mandatory comma-separated stable Authentik UID set.
DSH_SSO_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS is a mandatory comma-separated concrete IP CIDR set;
no forwarded address header is trusted. Mapped IPv6 peers match IPv4 CIDRs;
write mapped networks as native IPv4 CIDRs. Duplicate or malformed identity,
Host, Origin and Cookie headers fail closed. Host and Origin are never rewritten.
DSH_SSO_MAX_CONNECTION_SECONDS defaults to 900 and bounds every admitted upgrade;
its positive integer value must fit a Node timer. Admission always requires
external identity, even with valid native browser/API cookies. This is a shared
owner harness, not a multiuser authorization boundary.

The native Connection requestRejection fence executes before cookie exchange.
Native 403 stays 403. On 401 only, authenticatedUrl and authorizeIndex exchange a
native cookie internally, with the real Host/Origin. No launch URL or token is
returned, logged or configured by this package. Native TLS decides Secure.
HTTP responses append Set-Cookie; upgrades can internally bootstrap admission
without exposing authentication URLs, with cookies persisted by the next HTTP
request. Native Connection owns all API/WS protocol and lifecycle behavior.

Exec readiness connects to /tmp/dsh-sso-ready.sock and requires exactly ready
followed by newline. This UID-owned mode 0600 Unix socket has no public route;
it answers only while the gate is registered and the Host has a bound port.
Disposal removes the socket. There is no unauthenticated HTTP health exception.

The exact-source manager patch adds this package to native protectedModules,
so row disable and bundle deselection/removal are management-required; direct
installation/update of protected module names is denied. Rootfs packaging must
pin host-webserver, client-connection, plugin-manager, app-boot and this package;
prevent writable profile dependencies from shadowing those modules. Independent
market managers require the same policy. These are required packaging controls,
not a sandbox against an owner who can execute arbitrary harness code.
Hot uninstall or dependency reload must dispose the gate before replacement;
with this package absent the patched Host denies all routes instead of exposing
the native launch-token route. Do not replace the patched Host at runtime.

Tavern corresponding source
--------------------------
When DSH_SOURCE_ARCHIVE=/opt/dsh-source/tavern.tar.gz and DSH_SOURCE_URL names
the public HTTPS revision of this distribution, startup validates the archive.
The exact GET/HEAD /distribution/source.tar.gz route streams that immutable
archive behind the same mandatory guard (other methods 405). tapIndex adds
visible Tavern AGPL source-download and distribution-revision links. No source
route or notice is registered when neither variable is configured. The archive
is provided by immutable packaging; persistent user data is never archived.
